        </pre>
        <p class="caption">Confirmed source relationships, simplified to the components relevant to the analytical problem.</p>
      </div>
      <h3>Current stores and characteristics</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Solution context - table 4"><thead><tr><th>Store</th><th>Characteristics</th><th>Architectural issue</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Team B Document Database</td><td>A source-specific volume of article-level documents with a source-specific average record size; batch at at an organisation-specific daily time plus real-time Event Streaming Platform events for stock, saleability, and product updates.</td><td>Richest current Data Science attribute set, but squad-owned and not the strategic analytical platform.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Team C Relational Database / Time-series Database</td><td>Timestamp primary key, 24-hour chunks, multiple typed columns, JSONB catch-all, and separate Category/ProductCategory structures. a short rolling window.</td><td>Good extensibility pattern but limited history and maintained outside the shared analytical platform.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Search Search Platform</td><td>Populated from Product Aggregation Service; broad text fields used for real-time query matching and offline tests.</td><td>Optimised for search serving, not governed historical analytics.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Analytics Platform product data</td><td>A source-specific set of columns dominated by ERP merchandising/logistics data; hierarchy and internal keys available.</td><td>Does not contain the full enriched Product Aggregation Service representation or exposed Product Information Platform selling hierarchy required by Data Science.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
      <h3>Cross-cutting pain points</h3>
      <ul><li>No single glossary or authoritative identifier reference.</li><li>Product IDs use different names across systems and often require undocumented leading-zero removal.</li><li>Clickstream contains product-level ID plus colour name; deriving the article-level ID depends on a Document Database lookup.</li><li>Each squad independently cleans and transforms product data.</li><li>Adding attributes requires engineering intervention or separate schema work.</li><li>No consistent Data Quality Framework checks, operational run visibility, or failure management.</li></ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="src-solution-context-data-context">
      <h2>7. Data domains and source context</h2>
      <h3>Data domains required</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Solution context - table 5"><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Representative content</th><th>Primary analytical value</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Identifiers</td><td>Product Information Platform ID, Article ID, SKU ID, UPC/EAN, legacy grouping key, <code>internal_product_key</code>.</td><td>Joins, grain control, lineage, transaction and clickstream integration.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Hierarchies</td><td>ERP buying hierarchy L1-L8; Product Information Platform selling hierarchy; categories, breadcrumbs, and navigation.</td><td>Aggregation, merchandising context, model targets, online-path alignment.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Descriptive attributes</td><td>Colour, size, brand, fit, fabric, composition, body fit, product definition, style and shape.</td><td>Feature engineering, similarity, discovery, classification, search matching.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Commerce</td><td>Price, promotions, stock/availability, saleability, new-in dates.</td><td>Availability-aware training, historical reconstruction, campaign and recommendation eligibility.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Experience and media</td><td>Reviews; main, cutout, fabric, alternative images, and video.</td><td>Ranking, content quality, modelling, offline evaluation, future feature discovery.</td></tr>
