  ARTICLE2 -. "mapped for analytics" .-&gt; DPK
        </pre>
      </div>
      <h3>Required identifier controls</h3>
      <ul><li>Canonical identifier names and data types.</li><li>Explicit grain column or separate grain-specific entities.</li><li>No destructive loss of source identifiers; retain raw and cleaned representations.</li><li>Rules for leading-zero normalisation and prefix handling.</li><li>Validity dates for non-durable mappings such as legacy grouping key and barcode relationships.</li><li>Uniqueness, nullability, and referential-integrity checks per identifier.</li><li>Documented joins to transactions and clickstream.</li></ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="src-solution-context-requirements">
      <h2>9. Requirements catalogue</h2>
      <h3>Functional and data requirements</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table class="req-table" aria-label="Solution context - table 7"><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Priority / status</th><th>Source context</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>FR-01</td><td>Provide a unified analytical product catalogue serving Consumer Team A, Consumer Team B, and Consumer Data Science Team C.</td><td><span class="tag confirmed">Confirmed</span></td><td>Core project intent.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FR-02</td><td>Use Article ID as the standard working analytical grain/key unless a multi-grain model is approved.</td><td><span class="tag confirmed">Confirmed need</span><br><span class="tag decision">Model decision</span></td><td>All three squads confirmed Article ID as their working grain.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FR-03</td><td>Expose clean identifiers without leading zeros while preserving traceability to raw identifiers.</td><td><span class="tag confirmed">Confirmed</span></td><td>Repeated cross-squad pain point.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FR-04</td><td>Provide Product Aggregation Service attributes needed for Data Science, including the ability to discover and adopt new attributes.</td><td><span class="tag confirmed">Confirmed</span><br><span class="tag decision">Coverage decision</span></td><td>Users requested broad or complete Product Aggregation Service coverage.</td></tr>
