      <h3>Target-state principles</h3>
      <ol><li><strong>Authoritative-source alignment:</strong> obtain approval for every source and record why it is authoritative for each attribute domain.</li><li><strong>Raw before curated:</strong> retain source payload and ingestion metadata before consumer transformations.</li><li><strong>Stable consumer contract:</strong> expose canonical names, types, grains, and semantic definitions independent of upstream naming.</li><li><strong>History by design:</strong> make point-in-time analysis a first-class capability, not an afterthought.</li><li><strong>Extensibility with governance:</strong> support new fields rapidly without silently changing model contracts.</li><li><strong>Batch/real-time separation:</strong> do not make the analytical product part of the customer-facing serving critical path.</li><li><strong>Observable and owned:</strong> define quality, service levels, support, and lineage before migration.</li></ol>
    </section>

