    <section class="section" id="src-solution-context-data-management">
      <h2>12. Data model, history, quality, and metadata</h2>
      <h3>Candidate model options</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Solution context - table 9"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Strengths</th><th>Limitations</th><th>Assessment</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Single flat Article-level table</td><td>Simple for consumers; aligns with the common working grain.</td><td>Repeats SKU/category data or omits lower-grain attributes; wide schema.</td><td>Viable consumer view, but insufficient as the complete canonical model.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Separate Product, Article, and SKU entities</td><td>Explicit grain, better integrity, reduced duplication, supports barcode and stock relationships.</td><td>Requires joins and stronger consumer guidance.</td><td><span class="tag proposed">Preferred canonical direction</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Star schema</td><td>Familiar analytical structure and efficient dimensional joins.</td><td>May be cumbersome for evolving semi-structured attributes and point-in-time reconstruction.</td><td>Consider for published marts, not necessarily the ingestion/conformance core.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Typed columns plus governed semi-structured attributes</td><td>Stable important fields plus rapid source coverage and discovery.</td><td>Requires rules for promotion into typed fields, schema drift, and query performance.</td><td><span class="tag proposed">Recommended complementary pattern</span></td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
      <h3>Recommended logical publication set</h3>
      <ul><li><strong>Product current:</strong> consumer-friendly latest product/article view.</li><li><strong>Product daily history:</strong> dated snapshot with load and source timestamps.</li><li><strong>Product identifier map:</strong> all raw and canonical identifiers with grain and effective dates.</li><li><strong>Product SKU:</strong> size-level attributes where needed.</li><li><strong>Product category relationship:</strong> many-to-many categories, breadcrumbs, and <code>is_master_category</code>-equivalent designation.</li><li><strong>Product extended attributes:</strong> governed semi-structured source representation.</li></ul>
      <h3>Minimum quality rules</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Solution context - table 10"><thead><tr><th>Quality dimension</th><th>Illustrative control</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Completeness</td><td>Expected products, mandatory Article IDs, hierarchy coverage, country coverage, required critical fields.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Uniqueness</td><td>Uniqueness at declared grain; detect duplicate Article/day and SKU/day records.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Validity</td><td>Permitted prefixes, ID formats, country codes, timestamps, and domain values.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Referential integrity</td><td>SKU-to-Article, Article-to-Product Information Platform, category relationships, hierarchy nodes, and key mappings.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Freshness</td><td>Daily batch published within the agreed window; upstream timestamp and event lag measured.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Reconciliation</td><td>Counts and critical-field distributions compared with approved sources and prior periods.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Historical continuity</td><td>No missing snapshot dates; explicit rerun/correction status.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
      <h3>Metadata requirements</h3>
      <ul><li>Business definition, grain, source, owner, type, nullability, and sensitivity per field.</li><li>Transformation and identifier-normalisation rules.</li><li>Lineage from source APIs/tables to published datasets.</li><li>Freshness, retention, and quality expectations.</li><li>Example values and joins for Data Science consumers.</li><li>Change log and deprecation policy.</li></ul>
    </section>

