    <section class="section" id="src-solution-context-governance">
      <h2>14. Governance, security, and approval context</h2>
      <h3>Required approvals</h3>
      <ul><li><strong>Requirements approval:</strong> sponsor or key business stakeholder plus Architect and/or Technical Lead.</li><li><strong>Design Authority:</strong> required for major changes where confirmed by the Domain or Project Architect; record code, date, and architect.</li><li><strong>Data Governance:</strong> required for new data sharing, classification, and access/DAM-package changes.</li><li><strong>Information Security:</strong> existing-flow additions may not require a separate approval, but the TPM/Technical Lead must confirm. An Implementation Plan and InfoSec support request may be required.</li></ul>
      <h3>Security design considerations</h3>
      <ul><li>Product data is likely low sensitivity, but classification must be formally recorded rather than assumed.</li><li>Source API authentication includes an Authentication Service header; secrets must be held in an approved secret-management mechanism.</li><li>Access should be granted through governed groups/packages with separation between engineering write access and consumer read access.</li><li>Retain audit evidence for source access, dataset publication, permission changes, and material schema changes.</li><li>Review internal endpoints and repository references before reproducing them in broadly accessible documentation.</li></ul>
