    <section class="section" id="src-solution-context-appendix">
      <h2>19. Supporting technical context</h2>
      <h3>Product Aggregation Service behaviour described in the source</h3>
      <ul><li>Assembly combines Enriched Product, Commerce Inventory, Commerce Price, Reviews, Navigation, Promotions, and Specialist Product APIs.</li><li>Enriched Product and Commerce Price are described as base components; Product Aggregation Service may not return a response if either is unavailable.</li><li>In-memory caching is described as six hours; a 15-minute Edge Platform production cache is also referenced for Product Aggregation Service queries.</li><li>Stock indicators are provided at multiple product levels.</li><li>Different country codes are supported.</li><li>Traffic is described as split across Cloud Platform active/active environments through API Gateway configuration.</li><li>The documented public operation is a GET-style product-data request using product ID and country code; precise internal URLs and versions must be verified from authoritative API specifications.</li></ul>
      <h3>Product Information Platform and enterprise terminology</h3>
      <ul><li>Department ID corresponds to level 5 in the ERP hierarchy; a Category A &amp; Home example begins with <code>G5</code>.</li><li>Parent ID is the immediate parent of legacy grouping key and corresponds to level 8 in the ERP hierarchy.</li><li>The merchandising/buying hierarchy differs from the Product Information Platform selling hierarchy used online.</li><li>Stock and orders are managed at the enterprise Product ID / ERP Variant Article level.</li><li>Price and promotions are maintained at product/SKU level in the described online context.</li><li>A display set groups articles and uses an ID beginning with <code>ALT1</code>; its price range is derived from member article prices rather than summed.</li></ul>
      <h3>Existing documentation referenced by the source</h3>
      <ul><li>Product Terms.</li><li>Product Aggregation Service API documentation and API Specification/API Console.</li><li>Enriched Product schema repository.</li><li>Detailed Platform Attribute Mapping document - intentionally excluded from this document.</li><li>Product Information Platform functional requirements and Product Information Platform Analytics / Analytics Platform functional requirements.</li><li>Project planning, Work Tracker, operations, process, mapping, middleware, and source-team documentation.</li></ul>
