    <section class="section" id="src-drd-functional">
      <h2>10. Functional and data requirements</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Data requirements document - table 9"><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Status</th><th>Missing detail</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td class="id">FR-01</td><td>The solution shall provide one central analytical product catalogue for Consumer Team A, Consumer Team B and Consumer Data Science Team C.</td><td><span class="status confirmed">Confirmed</span></td><td>Physical output and access pattern are architecture decisions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="id">FR-02</td><td>The solution shall provide Product Aggregation Service attributes required for Data Science consumption.</td><td><span class="status partial">Partial</span></td><td>Approved field inventory and completeness rule.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="id">FR-03</td><td>The solution shall expose product identifiers without the existing leading-zero friction.</td><td><span class="status partial">Partial</span></td><td>Exact normalisation rules and whether raw values must also be exposed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="id">FR-04</td><td>The solution shall provide documented mappings between relevant product identifiers.</td><td><span class="status partial">Partial</span></td><td>Required identifier set, validity dates and acceptance tests.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="id">FR-05</td><td>The solution shall make ERP buying hierarchy L1-L8 available with product data.</td><td><span class="status confirmed">Confirmed</span></td><td>Required fields and historical semantics.</td></tr>
