    <section class="section" id="src-drd-history">
      <h2>11. Historical-data requirements</h2>
      <h3>Confirmed requirements</h3>
      <ul><li>Product data shall be refreshed and captured daily.</li><li>History is required for back-testing, offline evaluation and training using past product relationships.</li><li>Historical analysis must include products that may no longer be available.</li><li>Consumer Team B requires the ability to determine what was active and in stock on a historical day.</li></ul>
      <div class="callout conflict-box"><strong>Retention conflict:</strong> Consumer Team B requests [agreed history period] of history; Search requests [agreed history period]. The non-functional section states a minimum of [agreed history period]. No approved product-level retention commitment exists.</div>
      <div class="diagram"><div class="diagram-title">Required point-in-time question</div>
        <pre class="mermaid">
timeline
  title "Product state required for historical modelling"
  "Day D-2" : "Product attributes, hierarchy, activity and stock state"
  "Day D-1" : "Product attributes, hierarchy, activity and stock state"
  "Day D" : "Product attributes, hierarchy, activity and stock state"
  "Today" : "Latest product state"
        </pre>
      </div>
      <h3>Missing historical rules</h3>
      <ul><li>Approved retention: two or [agreed history period].</li><li>Which domains are snapshotted: descriptive attributes, categories, price, stock, promotions, reviews and media.</li><li>Snapshot cut-off time, time zone and business-date derivation.</li><li>Late-arriving updates and restatement rules.</li><li>Correction versus immutable-publication policy.</li><li>Handling of deleted/inactive products.</li><li>History start date and backfill requirements.</li><li>Required query performance for historical access.</li></ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="src-drd-quality">
      <h2>12. Data quality, reconciliation and monitoring requirements</h2>
      <h3>Confirmed need</h3>
      <p>Data quality checks and pipeline monitoring shall be applied. Data Quality Framework is referenced for consideration. Existing consumer product-data pipelines do not have a common Data Quality Framework framework; Consumer Team B currently uses basic counts, Monitoring Tool metrics and email alerts.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Data requirements document - table 10"><thead><tr><th>Quality area</th><th>Requirement status</th><th>Missing specification</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Completeness</td><td><span class="status partial">Required, not defined</span></td><td>Critical fields, tolerated nulls, record coverage and thresholds.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Uniqueness</td><td><span class="status partial">Implied by identifier issues</span></td><td>Uniqueness rules per grain and business date.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Validity</td><td><span class="status partial">Required, not defined</span></td><td>ID formats, prefixes, domains, countries and valid values.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Referential integrity</td><td><span class="status partial">Required by joins</span></td><td>Required Product-Article-SKU-category relationships and tolerances.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Freshness</td><td><span class="status partial">Daily required</span></td><td>Publication deadline, source lag and stale-data policy.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Reconciliation</td><td><span class="status partial">Count comparison exists today</span></td><td>Authoritative source, measures, tolerances and reconciliation grain.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Historical continuity</td><td><span class="status partial">Implied by daily history</span></td><td>Missing-date rule, restatement and exception process.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Distribution/anomaly monitoring</td><td><span class="status missing">Not specified</span></td><td>Metrics, baselines and severity.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
      <div class="diagram"><div class="diagram-title">Required quality-control lifecycle</div>
        <pre class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
  INPUT["Source batch"] --&gt; VALIDATE["Quality and contract checks"]
  VALIDATE --&gt;|"Pass"| PUBLISH["Publish daily product data"]
  VALIDATE --&gt;|"Warning"| POLICY["Missing: warning policy"]
  VALIDATE --&gt;|"Critical failure"| FAIL["Missing: hold, quarantine or publish policy"]
  PUBLISH --&gt; MONITOR["Freshness and reconciliation monitoring"]
  POLICY --&gt; MONITOR
  FAIL --&gt; ALERT["Missing: owner, alert route and recovery target"]
        </pre>
      </div>
      <h3>Monitoring information missing</h3>
      <ul><li>Named on-call/service owner.</li><li>Severity classification.</li><li>Alert channels and escalation path.</li><li>Detection and recovery targets.</li><li>Consumer notification rules.</li><li>Rerun, replay and partial-publication procedures.</li><li>Quality-result retention and audit requirements.</li></ul>
    </section>

