  <div class="source-content"><div class="source-furniture"><strong>Original header:</strong> consumer analytics PRODUCT CATALOGUE | REQUIREMENTS BASELINE<br><strong>Original footer:</strong> Draft v0.1 | Page</div><p><strong>STAKEHOLDER REQUIREMENTS BASELINE</strong></p><p><strong>Generic Product Catalogue</strong></p><p>Validation questionnaire and workshop template</p><div class="table-label">Table 1</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Requirements baseline template v0.1 (Word) - table 1"><tr><th><p><strong>Prepared for</strong></p></th><th><p>Consumer Team A, Consumer Team B, Consumer Team C, Consumer Data Engineering Function, Analytics Platform, Product Aggregation Service/Product Information Platform, Product and Governance stakeholders</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Document owner</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Enter accountable owner]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Response deadline</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Enter date]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Validation workshop</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Enter date, time and location/link]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Status</strong></p></td><td><p>Draft for stakeholder completion - not an approved requirements baseline</p></td></tr></table></div><div class="table-label">Table 2</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Requirements baseline template v0.1 (Word) - table 2"><tr><th><p><strong>Purpose. </strong>Use this document to confirm the business request, consumer use cases, scope, data grain, identifiers, attributes, history, service expectations, quality, governance and migration acceptance criteria. Completion should provide the evidence needed to baseline requirements before the High-Level Design is approved.</p></th></tr></table></div><div class="table-label">Table 3</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Requirements baseline template v0.1 (Word) - table 3"><tr><th><p><strong>Important. </strong>This document validates requirements; it does not ask stakeholders to select a physical technology or approve an implementation design. Where teams disagree, record each position and assign an accountable decision owner.</p></th></tr></table></div><h4>How to complete</h4><ol><li>Each stakeholder team completes its relevant consumer section before the validation workshop.</li><li>For every pre-populated statement, select Confirmed, Change required, Unresolved or Not applicable.</li><li>Replace every bracketed response prompt that applies to your team. Attach evidence or examples where available.</li><li>Use the workshop to reconcile conflicts, assign decisions and agree named acceptance owners.</li><li>The accountable business owner and Architecture/Technical Lead approve the consolidated baseline on the final page.</li></ol><h4>Baseline completion test</h4><div class="table-label">Table 4</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Requirements baseline template v0.1 (Word) - table 4"><tr><th><p><strong>Required outcome</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Complete when</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>Consumer need</p></td><td><p>All three Data Science teams have prioritised use cases and measurable acceptance criteria.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Scope</p></td><td><p>In-scope and out-of-scope boundaries are explicitly confirmed.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Semantics</p></td><td><p>Product, Article and SKU grains and identifier rules are agreed or have named decision owners.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Data coverage</p></td><td><p>Critical attributes, countries, hierarchies and history needs are prioritised.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Service</p></td><td><p>Freshness, retention, quality, recovery and change expectations are measurable.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Ownership</p></td><td><p>Business, product, technical, source and acceptance owners are named.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Approval</p></td><td><p>Conflicts and open decisions are resolved or formally carried into the HLD with due dates.</p></td></tr></table></div><h3>1. Respondent and review context</h3><p>Complete this page once per stakeholder response. The consolidated version should retain the identity of contributors and evidence supplied.</p><div class="table-label">Table 5</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Requirements baseline template v0.1 (Word) - table 5"><tr><th><p><strong>Responding team</strong></p></th><th><p><em>[Enter team or function]</em></p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Primary respondent</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Enter name and role]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Additional contributors</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Enter names and roles]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Response date</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Enter date]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Authority represented</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Business / Product / Data Science / Engineering / Source system / Governance / Security / Architecture]</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Evidence supplied</strong></p></td><td><p><em>[Links, dataset names, model documents, dashboards, API/schema references or examples]</em></p></td></tr></table></div><p><strong>1.1  What outcomes should this initiative produce for your team?</strong></p><p><strong>Please include: </strong>current friction, business or model outcome, expected benefit and how success could be measured</p><p><strong>Select one:  [ ] Confirmed   [ ] Change required   [ ] Unresolved   [ ] Not applicable</strong></p><div class="table-label">Table 6</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Requirements baseline template v0.1 (Word) - table 6"><tr><th><p><em>[Enter response here]</em></p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p></th></tr></table></div><p><strong>1.2  What would make this initiative unsuccessful for your team?</strong></p><p><strong>Please include: </strong>missing fields, incorrect grain, insufficient history, freshness, performance, access, trust or migration constraints</p><p><strong>Select one:  [ ] Confirmed   [ ] Change required   [ ] Unresolved   [ ] Not applica