  <h2>Stakeholder requirements baseline questionnaire</h2>
  <div class="source-file">generic-product-catalogue-stakeholder-requirements-baseline.docx</div>
  <div class="source-content"><div class="source-furniture"><strong>Attachment reconciliation:</strong> 4 diagram definition(s) absent from the Word file were restored from the attached text copy. Matching prose and tables were not duplicated.</div><div class="source-furniture"><strong>Original header:</strong> consumer analytics PRODUCT CATALOGUE<br><strong>Original footer:</strong> Draft for stakeholder validation | [Project date removed]</div><p><strong>Generic Product Catalogue</strong></p><p>Stakeholder Requirements Baseline Questionnaire</p><div class="table-label">Table 1</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Stakeholder requirements baseline questionnaire - table 1"><tr><th><p><strong>Status</strong></p></th><th><p>Draft for stakeholder validation</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Document owner</strong></p></td><td><p>[Enter accountable owner]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Response deadline</strong></p></td><td><p>[Enter date]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Validation workshop</strong></p></td><td><p>[Enter date and meeting details]</p></td></tr></table></div><h3>Stakeholder Requirements Baseline Questionnaire</h3><p><strong>Document status:</strong> Draft for stakeholder validation</p><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Establish an agreed requirements baseline before completing the High-Level Design</p><p><strong>Response deadline:</strong> [Enter date]</p><p><strong>Validation workshop:</strong> [Enter date and meeting details]</p><p><strong>Document owner:</strong> [Enter accountable owner]</p><h3>1. Purpose of this document</h3><p>This questionnaire is intended to confirm:</p><ul><li>The business problem and expected outcomes.</li><li>Which consumers and use cases must be supported.</li><li>The meaning and grain of Product, Article and SKU data.</li><li>Required attributes, identifiers, countries and hierarchies.</li><li>Historical, freshness and point-in-time requirements.</li><li>Data quality and publication controls.</li><li>Ownership, service and migration expectations.</li><li>Unresolved decisions requiring accountable approval.</li></ul><p>The example answers are illustrative. They show the expected level of detail but must be replaced or confirmed by the responsible stakeholder.</p><h4>Response status</h4><p>For each requirement, select one:</p><ul><li>[ ] Confirmed</li><li>[ ] Change required</li><li>[ ] Unresolved</li><li>[ ] Not applicable</li></ul><h3>Part A — Context</h3><h3>2. As-is state</h3><pre class="mermaid attached-diagram" data-attachment-source="pasted-text.txt">flowchart LR
    PRODUCT_INFO["Product Information Platform&lt;br/&gt;Product content and selling hierarchy"]
    ERP["ERP / Product Lifecycle Platform&lt;br/&gt;Buying hierarchy and merchandising"]
    CONTENT_API["Product Content API"]
    GATEWAY["Product Aggregation Service&lt;br/&gt;Online product representation"]
    STOCK_API["Inventory"]
    PRICE["Price"]
    PROMO["Promotions"]
    REV["Reviews"]
    CATEGORY_API["Navigation"]
    DOCSTORE["Team B Document Database&lt;br/&gt;Batch and Event Streaming Platform updates"]
    PG["Team C Relational Database / Time-series Database"]
    ES["Search Search Platform"]
    ANALYTICS_PLATFORM["Analytics Platform&lt;br/&gt;Analytical platform"]
    SEARCH["Consumer Data Science Team A"]
    TEAM_B["Consumer Data Science Team B"]
    TEAM_C["Consumer Data Science Team C"]

    PRODUCT_INFO --&gt; CONTENT_API --&gt; GATEWAY
    STOCK_API --&gt; GATEWAY
    PRICE --&gt; GATEWAY
    PROMO --&gt; GATEWAY
    REV --&gt; GATEWAY
    CATEGORY_API --&gt; GATEWAY

    ERP --&gt; ANALYTICS_PLATFORM
    PRODUCT_INFO --&gt; ANALYTICS_PLATFORM

    GATEWAY --&gt; DOCSTORE
    GATEWAY --&gt; PG
    GATEWAY --&gt; ES

    DOCSTORE --&gt;|"Daily snapshot"| ANALYTICS_PLATFORM
    DOCSTORE --&gt; SEARCH
    DOCSTORE --&gt; TEAM_B
    ES --&gt; SEARCH
    PG --&gt; TEAM_C

    ANALYTICS_PLATFORM --&gt; SEARCH
    ANALYTICS_PLATFORM --&gt; TEAM_B
    ANALYTICS_PLATFORM --&gt; TEAM_C</pre><p>Product data currently travels through different operational and analytical routes.</p><ul><li>Product Information Platform is the ultimate source of much of the product content.</li><li>Product Aggregation Service combines enriched product content with inventory, price, promotion, reviews, navigation and other online data.</li><li>Search, Consumer Team B and Consumer Team C maintain or consume different Product Aggregation Service-derived stores.</li><li>Analytics Platform receives ERP, Product Lifecycle Platform and Product Information Platform data through a separate analytical path.</li><li>Rich Product Aggregation Service attributes are not consistently available in Analytics Platform.</li><li>Each Data Science team performs some combination of identifier cleaning, hierarchy joining, transformation and snapshotting.</li><li>Product identifiers have inconsistent names, formats and leading-zero rules.</li><li>Historical coverage, data-quality controls, monitoring and documentation differ between teams.</li></ul><p>Logical flow: Product Information Platform -&gt; CONTENT_API; STOCK_API -&gt; GATEWAY; PRICE -&gt; GATEWAY; PROMO -&gt; GATEWAY; REV -&gt; GATEWAY; CATEGORY_API -&gt; GATEWAY; ERP -&gt; Analytics Platform; Product Information Platform -&gt; Analytics Platform; GATEWAY -&gt; DOCSTORE; GATEWAY -&gt; PG; GATEWAY -&gt; ES; DOCSTORE -&gt; Analytics Platform; DOCSTORE -&gt; SEARCH; DOCSTORE -&gt; TEAM_B; ES -&gt; SEARCH; PG -&gt; TEAM_C; Analytics Platform -&gt; SEARCH; Analytics Platform -&gt; TEAM_B; Analytics Platform -&gt; TEAM_C</p><h4>Current-state problems</h4><div class="table-label">Table 2</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Stakeholder requirements baseline questionnaire - table 2"><tr><th><p><strong>Problem</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Current impact</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>Fragmented product data</p></td><td><p>Data Scientists use different databases and extracts for similar requirements.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Duplicated transformations</p></td><td><p>Identifier cleaning, hierarchy resolution and attribute preparation are repeated by each team.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Inconsistent identifiers</p></td><td><p>Article, SKU, product and Analytics Platform keys are named and formatted differently.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Inadequate history</p></td><td><p>Historical coverage ranges from daily snapshots to a short rolling storage.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Difficult attribute onboarding</p></td><td><p>New attributes frequently require bespoke engineering work.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Limited quality controls</p></td><td><p>There is no consistent shared quality-gate framework.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Limited observability</p></td><td><p>Pipeline failures, stale data and degraded quality are not consistently visible.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Unclear ownership</p></td><td><p>Product, technical, source and service responsibilities require confirmation.</p></td></tr></table></div><h3>3. Intended analytical boundary</h3><pre class="mermaid attached-diagram" data-attachment-source="pasted-text.txt">flowchart LR
