rt?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“We require Article-to-Product Information Platform, SKU-to-Article, Article-to-internal_product_key and Article-to-category mappings. Search also requires a documented method for joining clickstream product ID and colour to Article ID.”</p><h4>Question 9.3 — What are the approved identifier-cleaning rules?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“Article and SKU identifiers should be exposed as strings without leading zeros. The original source value must also be retained. Prefixes must not be removed or interpreted unless an approved business rule exists.”</p><h4>Question 9.4 — Which mappings change over time?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“Barcode, legacy grouping key, category and hierarchy mappings can change. These relationships require effective-from and effective-to dates so historical joins use the relationship valid on the relevant date.”</p><h3>Part F — Data coverage</h3><h3>10. Attributes, hierarchies and countries</h3><div class="table-label">Table 8</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Stakeholder requirements baseline questionnaire - table 8"><tr><th><p><strong>Domain</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Representative content</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Priority</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Required grain/country</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Candidate source</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>Identifiers</p></td><td><p>Product Information Platform, Article, SKU, EAN, legacy grouping key, internal_product_key</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Buying hierarchy</p></td><td><p>ERP hierarchy L1–L8</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Selling hierarchy</p></t