    AUDIT["Published-data quality checks"]
    PUBLISH["Atomic publication"]
    HOLD["Hold or quarantine"]
    ALERT["Alert accountable owner"]

    SOURCE --&gt; RAW --&gt; VALIDATE
    VALIDATE --&gt;|"Pass"| CONFORM --&gt; AUDIT
    AUDIT --&gt;|"Pass"| PUBLISH
    VALIDATE --&gt;|"Fail"| HOLD --&gt; ALERT
    AUDIT --&gt;|"Fail"| HOLD</pre><div class="table-label">Table 10</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Stakeholder requirements baseline questionnaire - table 10"><tr><th><p><strong>Dimension</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Example control</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Threshold/severity</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Owner</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>Completeness</p></td><td><p>Mandatory Article IDs and critical-field coverage</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Uniqueness</p></td><td><p>No duplicate records at the declared grain</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Validity</p></td><td><p>Valid identifiers, country codes and timestamps</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Referential integrity</p></td><td><p>SKU-to-Article and Article-to-Product Information Platform relationships resolve</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Freshness</p></td><td><p>Dataset published by the agreed deadline</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Reconciliation</p></td><td><p>Counts and distributions reconcile to approved sources</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Historical continuity</p></td><td><p>No unexplained missing or duplicated dates</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Logical flow: SOURCE -&gt; RAW; VALIDATE -&gt; CONFORM; AUDIT -&gt; PUBLISH; VALIDATE -&gt; HOLD; AUDIT -&gt; HOLD</p><h4>Question 12.1 — Which failures should block publication?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“Publication must be blocked if Article ID uniqueness fails, more than 0.1% of SKUs lack an Article mapping, a required country is absent, or the product count falls by more than 10% without an approved source explanation.”</p><h4>Question 12.2 — What should consumers see when data is stale or degraded?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“The previous valid dataset should remain available with a visible stale status. Consumers should receive an alert containing the affected date, failed checks, current owner and expected recovery time.”</p><h4>Question 12.3 — What source-to-target reconciliation is required?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“Daily reconciliation should compare product and SKU counts by country, critical-field population, availability distribution and source update timestamps against Product Aggregation Service.”</p><h4>Question 12.4 — Who can release, hold or restate data?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“The on-call Data Engineering owner may hold publication. Releasing a degraded dataset requires approval from the Data Product Owner. Historical restatements require notification to all three Data Science acceptance owners.”</p><h3>Part I — Service, access and change</h3><h3>13. Non-functional requirements</h3><div class="table-label">Table 11</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Stakeholder requirements baseline questionnaire - table 11"><tr><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Requirement</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>Freshness</p></td><td><p>[Enter publication target and tolerated delay]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Availability</p></td><td><p>[Enter required query availability]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Performance</p></td><td><p>[Enter representative queries and response-time targets]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Recoverability</p></td><td><p>[Enter recovery and replay target]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Scalability</p></td><td><p>[Enter expected products, SKUs, countries and history growth]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Schema change</p></td><td><p>[Enter notice and compatibility requirements]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Observability</p></td><td><p>[Enter required dashboards, metrics and alerts]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Access</p></td><td><p>[Enter consumer, engineering and administrative groups]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Classification</p></td><td><p>[Enter sensitivity and audit requirements]</p></td></tr></table></div><h4>Question 13.1 — Which upstream changes must be communicated?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“Consumers must be notified of field additions, removals, renames, type changes, nullability changes, enumeration changes, grain changes and changes to business meaning.”</p><h4>Question 13.2 — How should breaking changes and deprecations be managed?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“Breaking changes require a new contract version, at least six weeks’ notice and a four-week overlap period. Each Data Science team must complete compatibility testing before the old version is removed.”</p><h4>Question 13.3 — Are there access, security or sharing restrictions?</h4><p><strong>Your answer:</strong></p><p>[Enter response]</p><p>Illustrative example - replace or confirm</p><p>“Data Scientists require read-only access through approved groups. Pipeline identities require write access only to their managed layers. Source credentials must not be exposed to consumers. Product data classification must be formally confirmed by Governance.”</p><h3>Part J — Ownership and migration</h3><h3>14. Ownership</h3><div class="table-label">Table 12</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Stakeholder requirements baseline questionnaire - table 12"><tr><th><p><strong>Responsibility</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Named owner</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Authority</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>Business requirements owner</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>Approves