  <h2>Attribute-authority matrix</h2>
  <div class="source-file">generic-product-catalogue-attribute-authority-matrix.docx</div>
  <div class="source-content"><div class="source-furniture"><strong>Attachment reconciliation:</strong> 3 diagram definition(s) absent from the Word file were restored from the attached text copy. Matching prose and tables were not duplicated.</div><div class="source-furniture"><strong>Original header:</strong> consumer analytics PRODUCT CATALOGUE<br><strong>Original footer:</strong> Draft for stakeholder validation | [Project date removed]</div><p><strong>Generic Product Catalogue</strong></p><p>Attribute-Authority Matrix and Decision Workbook</p><div class="table-label">Table 1</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Attribute-authority matrix - table 1"><tr><th><p><strong>Status</strong></p></th><th><p>Draft for stakeholder validation</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Document owner</strong></p></td><td><p>[Enter accountable owner]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Response deadline</strong></p></td><td><p>[Enter date]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Validation workshop</strong></p></td><td><p>[Enter date and meeting details]</p></td></tr></table></div><h3>Attribute-Authority Matrix</h3><p><strong>Phase:</strong> 2 — Source and attribute authority</p><p><strong>Status:</strong> Draft for profiling and stakeholder approval</p><p><strong>Document owner:</strong> [Enter owner]</p><p><strong>Decision deadline:</strong> [Enter date]</p><p><strong>Architecture reference:</strong> Generic Product Catalogue requirements baseline</p><h3>1. Purpose</h3><p>This artefact identifies the authoritative business owner, originating system, approved extraction interface and analytical source for every attribute required by the Generic Product Catalogue.</p><p>It is intended to prevent:</p><ul><li>Selecting one system as authoritative for every product attribute.</li><li>Treating a convenient analytical copy as the original authority.</li><li>Publishing conflicting values without a precedence rule.</li><li>Losing the distinction between raw, derived and manually governed attributes.</li><li>Building against an interface that has no contract or operational owner.</li><li>Using attributes at an incorrect Product, Article, SKU, country or historical grain.</li></ul><h3>Expected outcome</h3><p>When this matrix is complete:</p><ul><li>Every release-one attribute has an agreed business meaning.</li><li>Its grain and country context are explicit.</li><li>Its originating authority is known.</li><li>The approved ingestion interface is identified.</li><li>Update, deletion and historical behaviour are understood.</li><li>Conflicts have documented precedence rules.</li><li>Source, product and technical owners have approved the decision.</li></ul><h3>2. Important terminology</h3><h3>2.1 Business authority</h3><p>The person or domain accountable for the meaning and business rule of an attribute.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> The Commerce Price domain may own the definition of current selling price.</p><h3>2.2 System of record</h3><p>The system in which a fact is originally created or formally maintained.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> Product Information Platform may be the system of record for a product description.</p><h3>2.3 Authoritative interface</h3><p>The supported API, event, table or delivery contract through which the catalogue is approved to obtain the attribute.</p><p>The authoritative interface does not have to be the system-of-record database itself.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> Product Information Platform may be the system of record, while the Product Content API is the approved interface.</p><h3>2.4 Derived authority</h3><p>The approved process that calculates an attribute from other authoritative facts.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> article_is_saleable may be calculated from SKU saleability according to an approved aggregation rule.</p><h3>2.5 Analytical serving source</h3><p>The dataset through which Data Scientists consume the governed attribute.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> The Generic Product Catalogue in Analytics Platform is the analytical serving source. It is not necessarily the originating authority.</p><h3>2.6 Current source</h3><p>The database, extract or pipeline from which a consumer obtains the attribute today. A current source may be a copy rather than an authority.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong> Team B Document Database may currently supply brand to a model, but Product Information Platform may remain the originating authority.</p><h3>3. Authority model</h3><pre class="mermaid attached-diagram" data-attachment-source="pasted-text.txt">flowchart LR
    OWNER["Business/domain owner&lt;br/&gt;Defines meaning and rules"]
    SOR["System of record&lt;br/&gt;Creates or maintains the fact"]
    INTERFACE["Authoritative interface&lt;br/&gt;Supported API, event or table"]
    RAW["Immutable catalogue landing&lt;br/&gt;Source payload and metadata"]
    DERIVE["Approved derivation&lt;br/&gt;Conformance and business rules"]
    PRODUCT["Generic Product Catalogue&lt;br/&gt;Governed analytical outputs"]
    CONSUMERS["Search, Consumer Team B&lt;br/&gt;and Consumer Data Science Team C"]

    OWNER --&gt; SOR
    SOR --&gt; INTERFACE
    INTERFACE --&gt; RAW
    RAW --&gt; DERIVE
    DERIVE --&gt; PRODUCT
    PRODUCT --&gt; CONSUMERS

    OWNER -. "Approves semantics" .-&gt; DERIVE
    OWNER -. "Approves contract" .-&gt; PRODUCT</pre><p>Logical flow: OWNER -&gt; SOR; SOR -&gt; INTERFACE; INTERFACE -&gt; RAW; RAW -&gt; DERIVE; DERIVE -&gt; PRODUCT; PRODUCT -&gt; CONSUMERS</p><p>An attribute-authority decision is incomplete if it identifies only a physical source. It must also establish meaning, grain, ownership, interface and change behaviour.</p><h3>4. Current source landscape</h3><pre class="mermaid attached-diagram" data-attachment-source="pasted-text.txt">flowchart TB
    subgraph AUTHORING["Product authoring and enterprise data"]
        PRODUCT_INFO["Product Information Platform&lt;br/&gt;Product content and selling hierarchy"]
        ERP["ERP / Product Lifecycle Platform&lt;br/&gt;Buying hierarchy, merchandising and logistics"]
    end

    subgraph DIGITAL["Digital product domains"]
        CONTENT_API["Product Content API"]
        STOCK_API["Stock API"]
        PRICE["Commerce Price API"]
        PROMO["Offers API"]
        REV["Reviews API"]
        CATEGORY_API["Category API"]
        SPECIALIST["Specialist Product API"]
        GATEWAY["Product Aggregation Service&lt;br/&gt;Aggregated online representation"]
    end

    subgraph CURRENT["Current analytical and serving copies"]
        DOCSTORE["Team B Document Database"]
        PG["Team C Relational Database / Time-series Database"]
        ES["Search Search Platform"]
        ANALYTICS_PLATFORM["Analytics Platform"]
    end

    PRODUCT_INFO --&gt; CONTENT_API --&gt; GATEWAY
    STOCK_API --&gt; GATEWAY
    PRICE --&gt; GATEWAY
    PROMO --&gt; GATEWAY
    REV --&gt; GATEWAY
    CATEGORY_API --&gt; GATEWAY
    SPECIALIST --&gt; GATEWAY

    ERP --&gt; ANALYTICS_PLATFORM
    PRODUCT_INFO --&gt; ANALYTICS_PLATFORM

    GATEWAY --&gt; DOCSTORE
