pport the expected extraction volume?</p></td><td><p>[0–5]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Reconciliation</p></td><td><p>Can catalogue output be reconciled to the source?</p></td><td><p>[0–5]</p></td></tr></table></div><h3>Scoring guidance</h3><ul><li><strong>5:</strong> Fully supported and evidenced.</li><li><strong>4:</strong> Supported with minor limitations.</li><li><strong>3:</strong> Usable, but an important gap requires mitigation.</li><li><strong>2:</strong> Material uncertainty or weakness.</li><li><strong>1:</strong> Poor fit.</li><li><strong>0:</strong> Unsupported or unavailable.</li></ul><p>A high score does not override business authority. An analytically convenient source must not be selected if its owner cannot confirm the attribute’s meaning.</p><h3>10. Source-precedence rules</h3><p>Complete this section whenever two sources expose the same or apparently similar attribute.</p><div class="table-label">Table 14</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Attribute-authority matrix - table 14"><tr><th><p><strong>Conflict ID</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Source A</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Source B</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Are meanings identical?</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Precedence rule</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Owner</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>CON-01</p></td><td><p>Brand</p></td><td><p>Product Information Platform</p></td><td><p>ERP/Analytics Platform</p></td><td><p>[Yes/No/TBD]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>CON-02</p></td><td><p>Category</p></td><td><p>Product Information Platform selling hierarchy</p></td><td><p>Category API</p></td><td><p>No—different business purposes expected</p></td><td><p>Retain separately under distinct names</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>CON-03</p></td><td><p>Availability</p></td><td><p>Stock API</p></td><td><p>Product Aggregation Service</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>CON-04</p></td><td><p>Product description</p></td><td><p>Product Information Platform/Product Content API</p></td><td><p>Product Aggregation Service</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>CON-05</p></td><td><p>Article identifier</p></td><td><p>Product Information Platform/Product Aggregation Service</p></td><td><p>Analytics Platform/ERP</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr></table></div><h3>Example precedence decision</h3><p><strong>Attribute:</strong> Category</p><p><strong>Decision:</strong> Do not select one category source as universally authoritative.</p><p><strong>Reason:</strong> ERP buying hierarchy, Product Information Platform selling hierarchy and online navigation categories answer different business questions.</p><p><strong>Publication rule:</strong> Publish them as separately named relationships and provide a documented master-breadcrumb projection for convenience.</p><h3>11. Authority decision workflow</h3><pre class="mermaid attached-diagram" data-attachment-source="pasted-text.txt">flowchart TD
    START["Inventory required attribute"]
    DEFINE["Confirm business definition"]
    GRAIN["Confirm grain, country and time semantics"]
    OWNER["Identify business/domain owner"]
