    CONTRACT --&gt; APPROVE --&gt; IMPLEMENT</pre><p>Logical flow: START -&gt; DEFINE; CONFLICT -&gt; CONTRACT; CONFLICT -&gt; PRECEDENCE; CONTRACT -&gt; APPROVE</p><h3>12. Required stakeholder validation</h3><h3>Product/Product Information Platform owner</h3><p>Confirm:</p><ul><li>Product, Article and SKU definitions.</li><li>Identifier creation, update and retirement rules.</li><li>Product-description and characteristic ownership.</li><li>Selling-hierarchy ownership.</li><li>Approved Product Information Platform or Enriched Product interface.</li><li>Schema-change and support process.</li></ul><p><strong>Example response:</strong></p><p>“Product Information Platform is authoritative for Product, Article and SKU identity and descriptive content. The Product Content API is the supported consumption interface. Schema changes require notification through the Product API change process.”</p><h3>ERP/merchandising owner</h3><p>Confirm:</p><ul><li>Buying hierarchy authority.</li><li>Department and legacy grouping key definitions.</li><li>Effective-date behaviour.</li><li>Analytics Platform conform model alignment.</li></ul><p><strong>Example response:</strong></p><p>“ERP is authoritative for buying hierarchy and department. Analytics Platform conform data is the approved analytical representation. legacy grouping key is not durable and must be effective-dated.”</p><h3>Product Aggregation Service owner</h3><p>Confirm:</p><ul><li>Which fields are copied, decorated or calculated.</li><li>Whether the interface is supported for batch analytical extraction.</li><li>Saleability semantics.</li><li>Country-specific behaviour.</li><li>Source timestamps, deletions, replay and contract versions.</li></ul><p><strong>Example response:</strong></p><p>“Product Aggregation Service aggregates multiple domain facts. It is authoritative only for its approved composite saleability rule, not for underlying Product Information Platform descriptions or source price facts.”</p><h3>Inventory, price, promotions, reviews and navigation owners</h3><p>Confirm:</p><ul><li>Attribute definitions.</li><li>Natural grain.</li><li>Country/channel scope.</li><li>Effective timestamps.</li><li>Approved interfaces.</li><li>History and deletion behaviour.</li></ul><p><strong>Example response:</strong></p><p>“The Stock API owns SKU-country stock status. Product Aggregation Service exposes a supported copy, but reconciliation remains against Inventory.”</p><h3>Data Science consumers</h3><p>Confirm:</p><ul><li>Required fields and grains.</li><li>Historical needs.</li><li>Whether current squad copies contain transformations not available upstream.</li><li>Acceptable source substitutions.</li><li>Model and migration validation criteria.</li></ul><p><strong>Example response:</strong></p><p>“Consumer Team B requires Article-level saleability derived from SKU-country facts. The current Document Database transformation must be preserved until an equivalent governed derivation is validated.”</p><h3>13. Decision log</h3><div class="table-label">Table 15</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Attribute-authority matrix - table 15"><tr><th><p><strong>Decision ID</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Decision</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Options considered</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Decision and rationale</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Approver</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Date</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>ADR-AAM-01</p></td><td><p>Authority for rich product content</p></td><td><p>Product Information Platform direct / Product Content API / Product Aggregation Service</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>ADR-AAM-02</p></td><td><p>Authority for saleability</p></td><td><p>Product Aggregation Service / Commerce / catalogue derivation</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>ADR-AAM-03</p></td><td><p>Authority for navigation relationships</p></td><td><p>Category API / Product Aggregation Service / squad copies</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>ADR-AAM-04</p></td><td><p>Approved source for buying hierarchy</p></td><td><p>ERP direct / Analytics Platform conform</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>ADR-AAM-05</p></td><td><p>Identifier precedence and cleaning</p></td><td><p>[Enter options]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>ADR-AAM-06</p></td><td><p>Use of current squad-owned stores</p></td><td><p>Transitional source / validation only / excluded</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr></table></div><h3>14. Completion checklist</h3><p>The attribute-authority phase is complete when:</p><ul><li>[ ] Every release-one attribute has a business definition.</li><li>[ ] Every attribute has an explicit grain.</li><li>[ ] Country and channel context are defined.</li><li>[ ] The originating business authority is named.</li><li>[ ] The system of record is identified.</li><li>[ ] The approved extraction interface is identified.</li><li>[ ] Copied and derived values are distinguished from original facts.</li><li>[ ] Source timestamps and effective-time behaviour are understood.</li><li>[ ] Update, deletion and late-change behaviour are understood.</li><li>[ ] Historical requirements are documented.</li><li>[ ] Conflicting sources have an approved precedence rule.</li><li>[ ] Required source contracts and service owners are identified.</li><li>[ ] Representative data has been profiled.</li><li>[ ] Critical quality and reconciliation rules are defined.</li><li>[ ] Business/domain owners have approved the relevant rows.</li><li>[ ] Architecture has approved the consolidated authority model.</li></ul><h3>15. Approval</h3><div class="table-label">Table 16</div><div class="table-wrap"><table aria-label="Attribute-authority matrix - table 16"><tr><th><p><strong>Approval role</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Name</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Decision</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Conditions</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Date</strong></p></th></tr><tr><td><p>Data Product Owner</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Approve/Conditional/Reject]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Product/Product Information Platform owner</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Approve/Conditional/Reject]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Product Aggregation Service owner</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Approve/Conditional/Reject]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>ERP/Merchandising owner</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Approve/Conditional/Reject]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Commerce/Inventory representative</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Approve/Conditional/Reject]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Consumer Data Engineering Function</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Approve/Conditional/Reject]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Data Science acceptance owners</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Approve/Conditional/Reject]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Architecture/Technical Lead</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Approve/Conditional/Reject]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td><td><p>[Enter]</p></td></tr></table></div><h3>Approval declaration</h3><p>The approvers confirm that the matrix identifies the best currently supported authority and interface for each in-scope attribute. Any unresolved authority, contract, history or ownership gaps are explicitly recorded with accountable owners and target dates.</p><p>Approval authorises these decisions to be used as inputs to source profiling, proof-of-concept work and the High-Level Design.</p></div>
